<task id="032" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-agreements-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-16 completion — summary-panel restore + 128KB payload budget + supersede/highest-turn protection</title>
    <phase>3 Durable Review</phase>
    <gate>blocked (deps 031)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Completes the durable-recall guarantee; edge-case correctness (caps, coexisting outputs) for legal work product; ComposeWorkspace/panel .tsx changes.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Specified edge-case engineering against verified constraints (cap value, highest-turn selection, FR-29 second layer).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>G</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>031</deps>
    <tags>compose, spaarkeai, frontend, durable-recall</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Close the FR-16 guarantee's three gaps. (1) SUMMARY-PANEL RESTORE: AgreementReviewSummaryPanel is fed ONLY from the
    live event today — on reopen it must repopulate from the re-materialized findings (rows + risk badges + overallRisk),
    not just the gutter. (2) 128KB BUDGET: an over-cap findings payload becomes a truncation marker the projection
    SKIPS — silently vanishing on reopen; chunk findings across outputs or budget the payload, and surface (never
    swallow) a truncated case. (3) COEXISTENCE: the materializer replays only the HIGHEST-turn compose output — a later
    draft-alternative must not evict findings durability, and supersede ("Try another") must never retract the findings entry.
  </prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Compose materialization pipeline, panel state, ledger payload management.</role>
  <goal>Reopen restores gutter + summary panel; big reviews survive the cap; findings durability survives coexisting/superseded edits.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Verified facts (HUB-R1-REVIEW §4): NdaReviewSummaryPanel fed only from the live PaneEventBus event
      (ComposeWorkspace.tsx:1577-1586); InlinePayloadCapBytes=128KB (SessionLedgerEntries.cs:50), truncation markers
      skipped by ProjectComposeOutputs (ChatEndpoints.cs:1326-1329); materializer selects targetLedgerRef or the single
      highest-turn output (ComposeWorkspace.tsx:1420-1422); FR-29 session-annotations store (:814-852 save-on-mutation,
      :731/:759 rehydrate) is the second durability layer for placed comments; POST /compose-outputs/supersede exists
      (ChatEndpoints.cs:1337-1408). Design options for coexistence: multi-select materialization (replay findings +
      latest edit outputs distinctly) vs relying on FR-29 for placed comments + findings re-read — choose deliberately,
      document. Chunking option: emit findings as multiple compose outputs (per-section groups) each under the cap.
      A long agreement with many quotedText findings plausibly exceeds 128KB — budget realistically.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx (materialization selection + panel feed)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/AgreementReviewSummaryPanel.tsx (restore path)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Sessions/SessionLedgerEntries.cs (cap)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="031" status="pending">routing + gating (findings land in the right session, classified)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The reopen guarantee is CLOSED: gutter AND summary panel AND overallRisk restore with zero LLM calls; a truncated payload is SURFACED (visible notice) — silent vanish is the named failure mode. Scope: all three gaps.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Chunked findings stay ADR-040-conformant (each output store-before-render, standard DTO shape); no new ledger entry types. Scope: chunking.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Supersede semantics: superseding an EDIT output must not touch findings outputs; findings are never superseded by edits. Scope: coexistence design.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Materialization completeness + payload management</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-030-pane-event-bus.md</file>
      <file>projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-agreements-r1/notes/HUB-R1-REVIEW-2026-07-30.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="FR-29 annotations layer" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx (~:814-852, :731-759)">The second durability layer — decide its role in coexistence deliberately.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor; measure a realistic worst-case findings payload (50-section agreement) against the cap; re-verify selection logic refs.</step>
    <step order="1">Design + document the coexistence model (multi-output replay vs FR-29-backed) and the chunking scheme; pick the simplest that meets the closed guarantee.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement summary-panel restore from re-materialized findings (rows, badges, overallRisk).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement chunking/budget + the visible truncated-case notice.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement coexistence: findings replay alongside the latest edit output; supersede leaves findings intact.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: reopen-full-restore, over-cap chunked review restores, findings+edit coexistence, supersede protection.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: 032 ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the closed guarantee cannot be met without changing the server projection/selection (ChatEndpoints), STOP and present the minimal server delta with §10 justification before implementing.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Zero-LLM reopen restore"><steps><step>Review a doc; reload the page/session with devtools network open</step></steps><expected>Gutter notes + summary rows + overallRisk restore; zero dispatch/LLM calls in the trace.</expected></test>
    <test name="Dark mode"><steps><step>Reopen in dark mode</step></steps><expected>Restored badges/rows use semantic tokens.</expected></test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools><tool name="npm">Compose lib build + tests</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">ComposeWorkspace.tsx + AgreementReviewSummaryPanel.tsx (restore + caps + coexistence)</output>
    <output type="test">reopen/cap/coexistence tests</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Reopen a reviewed doc: gutter notes AND summary-panel rows AND overallRisk all restore; zero LLM calls (network assert).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A synthetic &gt;128KB findings set restores completely via chunking (or the truncated case shows an explicit notice — never silent absence).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Run review → accept a draft-alternative → reload: findings AND the edit state both restore (highest-turn-only eviction fixed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Supersede an edit output → findings unaffected (ledger + UI proof).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a corrupted/partial chunk set surfaces a visible degraded-restore notice, not a crash.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-16 completion; HUB-R1-REVIEW §4 risks. With this task, "reopen restores the review deterministically" is fully true — the owner's Phase-3 leg.</notes>
  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
